From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:48:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] compat_tool: show the 2D window by default

Kettle Linux runs Lepton on handhelds with no headset, so a headless
launch shows nothing. Default APP_WANTS_FLATSCREEN to true; the
lepton-show-flatscreen marker and headless-* contexts keep working,
and APP_WANTS_FLATSCREEN=false in the environment restores headless.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 compat_tool/liblepton/app_metadata.sh | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compat_tool/liblepton/app_metadata.sh b/compat_tool/liblepton/app_metadata.sh
index 741d336..08f5ba3 100755
--- a/compat_tool/liblepton/app_metadata.sh
+++ b/compat_tool/liblepton/app_metadata.sh
@@ -155,6 +155,10 @@ APP_FLATSCREEN_FILE="${APP_DIR}/lepton-show-flatscreen"
 
 function app_wants_flatscreen()
 {
+    # Kettle: a handheld has no headset, so every app gets the 2D window unless the
+    # environment says otherwise (APP_WANTS_FLATSCREEN=false)
+    APP_WANTS_FLATSCREEN="${APP_WANTS_FLATSCREEN:-true}"
+
     if ! is_steamlaunch && ! is_app; then
         APP_WANTS_FLATSCREEN="true"
     fi
